{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data disclosure paradox data disclosure paradox","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md","fileName":"Data Disclosure Paradox.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Disclosure Paradox","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-17 09:48\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Ownership and Access Rights]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ownership and Access Rights","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data disclosure paradox data disclosure paradox","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md","fileName":"Data Disclosure Paradox.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Disclosure Paradox","heading":"Data Disclosure Paradox","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The data disclosure paradox claims that a prospective buyer cannot value information without seeing it, yet disclosure gives away what the seller hoped to sell. It is often used to argue that data markets need property-like protection.\n\nFor large datasets, the problem is weaker than it first appears. Samples, descriptions, contractual safeguards, and the difference between inspecting a portion and obtaining the complete resource can support valuation without transferring the full value.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ownership and Access Rights","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Disclosure Paradox.md","sourceType":"markdown","secti